# Localization

Never edit `Localizable.xcstrings` manually — Xcode auto-extracts on build. Languages: `en`, `vi`. Details: `docs/LOCALIZATION.md`.

Use **raw English text**, not dot-notation keys. Prefer `LocalizedStringKey` for SwiftUI view params; use `String(localized:)` only when you need an eagerly-resolved `String`. Do not type a field `LocalizedStringKey` if it carries runtime/data text (e.g. an event title from SwiftData).

```swift
// ❌ BAD
Text("settings.lunarSpecialDates.title")
let title: LocalizedStringKey = event.title  // data text is not a catalog key

// ✅ GOOD — SwiftUI literals (lazy LocalizedStringKey)
Text("Lunar Special Dates")
Label("Add Event", systemImage: "plus")
.navigationTitle("Settings")

// ✅ GOOD — need a String (interpolation, format, UIKit/alerts)
let msg = String(format: String(localized: "Giỗ %@ %@"), relation, name)
alert.title = String(localized: "Are you sure?")
```
